    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.git\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently `mini.git` opens a snapshot of the related file when visiting a `diff` buffer.\r\n\r\nI am wondering if when the diff is from the `HEAD`, e.g. `git diff`, or `git diff --HEAD`, then we can directly open the file so that we can review the diff and make the edit directly. This is a very convenient feature.\r\n\r\nThanks for your  awesome plugin, and consideration for this feature request.\r\n\r\nBest!",
