        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This is the snapshot of the HEAD of file, not the buffer associating with the file itself, so you cannot directly edit that buffer to change the file.\r\n\r\nThis is not a snapshot from the HEAD, but from the actual worktree (same *content* as you get from `:edit lua/minuet/config.lua`).\r\n\r\nBut I get what you mean, you can not use it to directly edit the file on the disk. This is rather deliberate because if it *is* editable, then the diff might get outdated and this is slightly confusing.\r\n\r\nTo actually edit the file, you can navigate to the closest from top file name (like a line '+++ b/lua/minuet/config.lua') and execute `gf` on the file part. I think even a custom function in this case can be rather concise.",
